--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-12 Start
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: The city had not altered much during my seven years of absence. The
      condition of the Binondo pavement, with the same holes in the road which I
      remembered as a schoolboy, was unchanged.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I immediately went to my home in Calamba. My first operation in the
      Philippines relieved the blindness of my mother, by the removal of a double
      cataract.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: This gave me fame, which brought patients from all parts of Luzon.
      I charged a moderate amount, even gave services to people who couldn't pay,
      for free. During my seven months' stay here, I made over 5,000 pesos. I now
      look back at the diamond ring that started it all, a memento from my dear sister
      Neneng. I will keep looking back at this as a reminder.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "Shortly after my arrival, Governor-General Terrero summoned me by
      telegraph to Malaca\xF1an from Kalamba. The interview proved to be due to the
      interest in the author of \u201CNoli Me Tangere\u201D and a curiosity to read
      the novel, arising from the copious extracts with which the Manila censors
      had submitted an unfavorable opinion when asking for the prohibition of the
      book."
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 6
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: General Terrero was afraid that I might get attacked by some of the
      many people who would feel themselves aggrieved by his plain picture of undesirable
      classes in the Philippines. He assigned to me a bodyguard, a young Spanish
      lieutenant named Jose Traviel de Andrade. We soon became friends, as we both
      had artistic and other tastes in common.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: A somewhat liberal administration was now governing the Philippines,
      and efforts were being made to correct the more glaring abuses in the social
      conditions. I took it upon myself to interest the people in the community to
      gather reliable statistics, to go thoroughly into the actual conditions, and
      to leave out the generalities which usually characterized Spanish documents.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I asked them to cooperate, pointing out that when they did not complain
      it was their own fault more than that of the government if they suffered injustice.
      I urged them to create truthful, reasonable statements, rather than exaggerate
      them, as it is foolish to do so. Describe the abuses that the people suffered,
      with evidence in a calm, factual manner.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I prepared a report that brings forward the grievances of the townsfolk,
      with special points that favour the community's industriousness, willing to
      help themselves, interest in education, and expressing confidence in a fair
      government, pointing out the fact that they were risking the displeasure of
      their landlords by furnishing the information requested.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 1
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Before I left for the Philippines again, I received numerous reports
      that a local festival was given to the Chinese as they paid a heftier sum.
      Claiming that since they are in their home country, they have prior consideration
      and are entitled to it by law. I learned of it and gave my approval as the
      people have a reasonable argument as to why.
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 2
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 618ec32722d755e4e80a7f213a9d80b0, type: 2}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I now sail to Hong Kong
    isLeftSide: 1
    pose: 0
